        "original_id": "429c0de6-7fe6-53e9-9efa-36b4172f7ed4",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Cosmopolitan, Cuba Libre, Bacardi Superior\n- Roles: Bartender\n- Concepts: Cocktails, cocktail ingredients\n\nFacts:\n- The Cosmopolitan, also called a cosmo, is a cocktail made with vodka, triple sec, cranberry juice, and freshly squeezed or sweetened lime juice.\n- The Cuba Libre is a caffeinated alcoholic cocktail made with cola, lime, and dark or light rum.\n- A bartender can generally mix classic cocktails such as a Cosmopolitan, Manhattan, Old Fashioned, and Mojito.\n- Bacardi Superior is a rum mostly used to make cocktails that call for white rum, including Cuba Libre, Daiquiri, Piña Colada, Mojito, and the Bacardi cocktail.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
